                  <additions>
                     <list>
                        
                        <item xml:id="a1">
                           <locus target="#128v"/>
                           <desc type="GuestText">A note on symbolic interpretation of the covenant made between Abraham and Abimelech (<ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT1367Exodus">Exodus 21:27–31</ref>). 
                              It is written with square letters by a mediocre hand.</desc>
                        <q xml:lang="gez">ወነሥአ፡ አብርሃም፡ አልህምተ፡ ወወሀቦሙ፡ ወአቀመ፡ ፸ አባግዓ፡ ባሕቲቶን፡ <gap reason="ellipsis" resp="AA"/></q>
                        <q xml:lang="en">Abraham took cows and gave them (to Abimelech). And he set seventy lambs by themselves …</q> </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="a2">
                           <locus target="#128v"/>
                        <desc type="GuestText">A short unidentified text on the purity and perpetual virginity of Mary. It is written in a very crude hand.</desc>                        
                           <q xml:lang="gez">አእሚሮ፡ ከሀሌ፡ ኵሉ፡ ከመ፡ ይለብስ፡ ሥጋ፡ እጓለ፡ እመሕያው፡ ፈጠራ፡ ለቅድስት፡ ድንግል፡ ውስተ፡ ከርሠ፡ እማ፡ <gap reason="ellipsis" resp="AA"/></q>
                           <q xml:lang="en">Knowing that He assumes the body of mankind, the Omnipotent created the Holy Virgin in the womb of her mother …</q>
                        </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="a3">
                           <locus target="#132v"/>
                           <desc type="GuestText">An excerpt from <title ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT2293Sawase">Sawāsǝw (general record)</title>  on types and qualities of precious stones (cp. <ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/EMML1543">EMML 1543 ff 32va–33va</ref>). 
                              The note is written in a fine hand, the same as <ref target="#a4"/>.</desc>
                           <quote xml:lang="gez">እጽሕፍ፡ ነገረ፡ አዕናቍ፡ ቀይሐን፡ ወኅብረ፡ ደም፡ ወጸዓዳን፡ ወሐመልሚላን፡ ወኅብረ፡ ስሞሙሂ፡ ጳዝዮን፡ <gap reason="ellipsis" resp="AA"/> </quote>
                           <quote xml:lang="en">I write the account of precious stones: red ones, those like blood, white ones, green ones whose common name is Ṗāzǝyon</quote>
                        </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="a4">
                           <locus target="#132v"/>
                           <desc type="GuestText">A note on the symbolic interpretation of Biblical peoples as different animals. The note is written in the same hand as <ref target="#a3"/>.</desc>
                           <q xml:lang="gez">ምሳሌ፡ አሕዛብ፡ አናብስት፡ ባቢሎን፡ አናምርት፡ ሚዶን፡ ድብ፡ ፋርስ፡ አዝዕብት፡ ግብጽ፡ አክልብት፡ ኢሎፍሊ፡ <gap reason="ellipsis" resp="AA"/></q>
                           <q xml:lang="en">Symbol of peoples: Babylon <supplied reason="subaudible">is like</supplied> Lion, Midon <supplied reason="subaudible">is like</supplied> tigers, Persia
                              <supplied reason="subaudible">is like</supplied> a bear, Egypt <supplied reason="subaudible">is like</supplied> hyenas, Philistines (ʾIlofli) <supplied reason="subaudible">are like</supplied> dogs.</q>
                        </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="e1">
                           <desc>The title of <ref target="#ms_i1"/>, <foreign xml:lang="gez">አእማደ፡ ምሥጢር፡</foreign> is crudely written on the front board with yellow paint.</desc>
